Subject: [PATCH] Core: check allocator size arithmetic before use

Reject nonzero sizes that cannot be aligned, and check mraw metadata
additions before accessing the allocation cache or changing metadata.
Reject unrepresentable append offsets before recycling chunk space.
Compare requests against remaining chunk capacity and check tail growth
before changing sanitizer state or calling realloc.

Preserve existing zero-size behavior and document the alignment helper's
zero return for unrepresentable results. Allocation entry points must
recognize that result as failure for a nonzero request. Add arithmetic-only
coverage for normal alignment and the representable size boundary,
including the non-inline wrapper.

This patch contains only the overflow fix; the mraw shrink-offset fix is
separate. With both fixes present, all 145 registered CTest tests passed
with AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, including optional
C++ coverage. Leak detection was disabled due to the sandbox's tracing.
The reporter's standalone reproducer was not run during this validation.

---
diff --git a/source/lexbor/core/mem.h b/source/lexbor/core/mem.h
--- a/source/lexbor/core/mem.h
+++ b/source/lexbor/core/mem.h
@@ -99,12 +99,23 @@
     return mem->chunk_length;
 }
 
+/* Returns zero for zero size or an unrepresentable aligned size. */
 lxb_inline size_t
 lexbor_mem_align(size_t size)
 {
-    return ((size % LEXBOR_MEM_ALIGN_STEP) != 0)
-           ? size + (LEXBOR_MEM_ALIGN_STEP - (size % LEXBOR_MEM_ALIGN_STEP))
-           : size;
+    size_t padding;
+    size_t remainder = size % LEXBOR_MEM_ALIGN_STEP;
+
+    if (remainder == 0) {
+        return size;
+    }
+
+    padding = LEXBOR_MEM_ALIGN_STEP - remainder;
+    if (size > SIZE_MAX - padding) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
+    return size + padding;
 }
 
 lxb_inline size_t
diff --git a/source/lexbor/core/mem.c b/source/lexbor/core/mem.c
